{
  "dom_id": "step-q155553",
  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14178066/assets/5a661c340c9eb953b93ceeebb23cd3d251a5591db3893a917f94f465c81bbffc.png)\n\nGiven that $r$, $s$ and $t$ in the above diagram are parallel, find $m∠1.$",
  "worked_solution": "Consider $∠2$ and $∠3$ in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14178066/assets/db08637378dcf3968cb0e526057212d7c673fb1818eb84db5f076eb9cf4fb2c9.png)\n\nNote that $∠2$ and the angle whose measure is ${110}^{∘}$ are corresponding angles formed by the same transversal. Therefore, \n\n$$\nm∠2={110}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, note that $∠3$ and the angle whose measure is ${45}^{∘}$ are corresponding angles formed by the same transversal. Therefore, \n\n$$\nm∠3={45}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nLet's add these measures to our diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14178066/assets/9420706692d49a3faf575d20be6b64f306d9fc901e477184e6b2f2ad21907d8f.png)\n\nThe angles $∠1$, $∠2,$ and $∠3$ combined give a straight angle. So, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠1+m∠2+m∠3 & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠1+{110}^{∘}+{45}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠1+{155}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠1 & ={25}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
